                <h2>Scenario Recap: One Video Ran for Three Weeks Before Budget Went to Waste</h2>
<p>In mid-February, a utility app's overseas operations team launched a new product on TikTok Shop. For the first two weeks, they followed their Douyin playbook—</p>
<p><strong>Problem</strong>: Only one primary creative was prepared and repeatedly投放. This video was well-edited with clear selling points, but after two weeks of running, CPM increased from $8 to $14 while conversion rate dropped from 3.2% to 1.1%. The team realized creative fatigue hit faster than expected.</p>
<p>They faced a typical cold launch dilemma: <strong>insufficient creative inventory caused the algorithm to lack enough learning samples, leading to skewed models and runaway costs.</strong></p>
<hr />
<h2>Diagnosis: Creative Fatigue Is a Symptom, Not the Root Cause</h2>
<p>The operations lead conducted a quick triage, eliminating three distractions:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Landing page issues ruled out</strong>: Independent site load speed was normal, with no abnormal drop-off in add-to-cart flow</li>
<li><strong>Product selection issues ruled out</strong>: Similar products showed stable conversion data on comparable influencer accounts</li>
<li><strong>Audience targeting issues ruled out</strong>: Broad targeting tests also showed rising costs</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Conclusion</strong>: The problem wasn't on the 投放 side—it was the creatives themselves. When a single piece of content exceeded 20,000 impressions to the same audience, user novelty faded, and TikTok's algorithm would classify it as "low-performing" and reduce推送.</p>
<p>Core contradiction: TikTok's traffic distribution relies on creative diversity, making single-asset marginal returns decline extremely fast.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Actions: Three Steps to Build a Dynamic Creative Library</h2>
<h3>Step 1: Deconstruct Selling Points to Build a Creative Skeleton</h3>
<p>The team broke down product selling points into 4 dimensions:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Feature Demo</strong> (showing actual product usage scenarios)</li>
<li><strong>Comparison/Review</strong> (Before/After or versus competitors)</li>
<li><strong>User Pain Point</strong> (focusing on specific struggles of target users)</li>
<li><strong>Social Proof</strong> (UGC testimonials, authentic reviews)</li>
</ol>
<p>Each dimension required at least 3 duration variants (6s hook, 15s full version, 30s in-depth). <strong>This step solved the "don't know what to create" blind spot.</strong></p>
<h3>Step 2: Batch Production to Reduce Single-Asset Weight</h3>
<p>Instead of obsessing over one high-quality production, they adopted a "mixed production" strategy:</p>
<ul>
<li>Internal operations quickly produced 6 feature demo creatives using Jianying</li>
<li>Recruited 2 mid-tier TikTok influencers (50K-200K followers) for custom testimonial versions</li>
<li>Used AI tools to batch-generate 4 subtitle + voiceover versions</li>
</ul>
<p>Total: 12 raw assets entered AB testing phase.</p>
<h3>Step 3: Data Tiering to Build Dynamic Elimination Mechanism</h3>
<p>The team established simple creative scoring criteria:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Scoring Dimension</th>
<th>Threshold</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>CTR (Click-Through Rate)</td>
<td>&gt; 1.5%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>3-Second Completion Rate</td>
<td>&gt; 40%</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Add-to-Cart Conversion</td>
<td>&gt; 2%</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Every 48 hours, the lowest-scoring creative was eliminated while new versions were added. <strong>This solved the "don't know when to stop" execution challenge.</strong></p>
<hr />
<h2>Results: 40% Cost Reduction, Extended Creative Lifespan</h2>
<p>After 3 weeks, the data comparison:</p>
<ul>
<li>Cost per conversion: Dropped from $12 to $7.2</li>
<li>Average creative lifespan: Extended from 2 weeks to 5 weeks</li>
<li>Stable running creatives: Increased from 1 to 8</li>
</ul>
<p>More importantly, the creative library formed a <strong>self-sustaining cycle</strong>: new creatives continuously replenished, underperformers automatically eliminated, and the team no longer needed to relaunch weekly.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Key Takeaways: During Cold Launch, Quantity Comes Before Quality</h2>
<p>For TikTok Shop cold launches, two recommendations:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Solve existence first, then excellence</strong>: Don't obsess over perfecting single creatives during the first two weeks. First ensure the creative library has 10-15 usable assets, giving the algorithm enough learning samples</li>
<li><strong>Establish data-driven iteration rhythm</strong>: Set clear elimination metrics and review cycles to avoid budget waste from "gut feeling" adjustments</li>
</ol>
<p>A creative library isn't a one-time project—it's an ammunition depot requiring continuous resupply.</p>
